    "q-146201": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146201",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{5}, & x=5 \\\\ \\frac{3}{5}, & x=10 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find the conditional variance $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=2]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)$ is shown above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|2}=8.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,2)]-{\\mu }_{X|2}^{2} \\\\  & =[(5)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{2}{5}+(10)^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{5}]-(8)^{2} \\\\  & =10+60-64 \\\\  & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
