    "q-145561": {
      "dom_id": "step-q145561",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "| $y$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ | $0.1$ | $0.4$ | $0.5$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1]$ given that the conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)$ is shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|1}=1.4.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=1] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,1)]-{\\mu }_{Y|1}^{2} \\\\  & =[(0)^{2}\\cdot 0.1+(1)^{2}\\cdot 0.4+(2)^{2}\\cdot 0.5]-(1.4)^{2} \\\\  & =0+0.4+2-1.96 \\\\  & =0.44.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
