    "q-146245": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146245",
      "name": "Question 7",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3]$ given that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{Y|3}=\\frac{1}{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $Y$ given $X=x$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=x] & =\\text{E}[(Y-{\\mu }_{Y|x})^{2}\\,|\\,X=x] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{Y}^{2}\\,|\\,X=x]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)]-{\\mu }_{Y|x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x),$ let's first find the marginal distribution for $X,$ corresponding to the row totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ | ${f}_{X}(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{2}{9}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{9}$ | $\\frac{4}{9}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{X}(x)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding row total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $Y$ given that $X=x:$\n\n| ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ | $Y=0$ | $Y=1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{2}{3}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=2$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{3}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[Y\\,|\\,X=3] & =[{\\sum }_{y}{y}^{2}\\,{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,3)]-{\\mu }_{Y|3}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{3}{4}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}]-{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
