    "q-146272": {
      "dom_id": "step-q146272",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nSuppose $X$ and $Y$ are discrete random variables. Find $\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4]$ given that the random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above and the corresponding conditional expected value is ${\\mu }_{X|4}=\\frac{4}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the conditional variance of $X$ given $Y=y$ is defined by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=y] & =\\text{E}[(X-{\\mu }_{X|y})^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y] \\\\  & =\\text{E}[{X}^{2}\\,|\\,Y=y]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2} \\\\  & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)]-{\\mu }_{X|y}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn order to find ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y),$ let's first find the marginal distribution of $Y,$ corresponding to the column totals: \n\n| $f$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{16}$ | $\\frac{3}{16}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{1}{4}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n| ${f}_{Y}(y)$ | $\\frac{5}{16}$ | $\\frac{11}{16}$ |\n\nThe conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y$ is\n\n$$\n{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)=\\frac{f(x,y)}{{f}_{Y}(y)}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, dividing each joint probability by the corresponding column total, we obtain the conditional probability mass function of $X$ given that $Y=y:$\n\n| ${f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,y)$ | $Y=4$ | $Y=8$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=0$ | $\\frac{1}{5}$ | $\\frac{3}{11}$ |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{4}{5}$ | $\\frac{8}{11}$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ |\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Var}[X\\,|\\,Y=4] & =[{\\sum }_{x}{x}^{2}\\,{f}_{X|Y}(x\\,|\\,4)]-{\\mu }_{X|4}^{2} \\\\  & =[{0}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{5}+{1}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{4}{5}]-{(\\frac{4}{5})}^{2} \\\\  & =0+\\frac{4}{5}-\\frac{16}{25} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{25}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
